Reading from zero to advanced electromagnetic study (@em-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q", #source "../sources/Electricity-and-Magnetism-MIT-8-02T.lingua#r_00CWY37VDJSBRF5D6A8BCD7SXT", #source "../sources/Fisica-III-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0A3ZH3ZNQ5PGJ4Y05BSSCBAJE7", #electromagnetism "Begin-with-an-electromagnetic-question.lingua#r_1PMJFESWTM62NGP42X33D125WA") { r_3PMR408MBJV3M39SCRZGR7S9RF
**Read:** [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q), chapters 5–16 in full, with exercises; [Electricity and Magnetism — MIT 8.02T and TEAL notes](../sources/Electricity-and-Magnetism-MIT-8-02T.lingua#r_00CWY37VDJSBRF5D6A8BCD7SXT), complete electricity/magnetism notes and corresponding course work; [Física III — Bernhard Johannes Lesche, UFJF](../sources/Fisica-III-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0A3ZH3ZNQ5PGJ4Y05BSSCBAJE7), the complete available Física III sequence.

Start by explaining an everyday observation: a battery lighting a lamp, a compass beside a wire, a charged object attracting paper, or a radio receiving a signal. Draw the physical arrangement and distinguish what was observed from the proposed model. The first reading introduces charge, force, voltage, current and magnetic field before demanding vector calculus.

Read the entire electricity/magnetism part of [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q) and the corresponding complete [Electricity and Magnetism — MIT 8.02T and TEAL notes](../sources/Electricity-and-Magnetism-MIT-8-02T.lingua#r_00CWY37VDJSBRF5D6A8BCD7SXT) notes. Use [Física III — Bernhard Johannes Lesche, UFJF](../sources/Fisica-III-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0A3ZH3ZNQ5PGJ4Y05BSSCBAJE7) as a Portuguese parallel and [Física Geral — Eletromagnetismo, UFRGS](../sources/Fisica-Geral-Eletromagnetismo-UFRGS.lingua#r_1PTBDGGV7JKZBV0RD53GDFXQ8C) where accessible. Work the questions, dimensional checks, diagrams and substantial end-of-chapter problems. Returning to a book at a later Record means extending the reading, not replacing the book with this guide.

The next complete technical spine is [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA) and [Electromagnetics Volume 2 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-2-Ellingson.lingua#r_5P52CZD00XV6MMPFY9RHADT5KJ), then all of [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1) and [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H) with the mathematical support of [Vector Calculus — David Tong](../sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5). [Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin](../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC), [Electromagnetic Fields and Energy — Haus and Melcher](../sources/Electromagnetic-Fields-and-Energy-Haus-Melcher.lingua#r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV) and [The Feynman Lectures on Physics, Volume II](../sources/Feynman-Lectures-Volume-II.lingua#r_436GYN2CVWCERX7EXFDTWX28XT) offer sustained engineering and physical comparisons. [A complete practical and academic programme](../study/A-complete-practical-and-academic-programme.lingua#r_4XEMVM6SXP5T369FTCJ14H53YX) makes the practical, graduate and research depth explicit. Keep a notebook of assumptions, independent derivations, failed explanations and revisions. No prior degree is assumed; the work becomes progressively demanding.

**Continue:** [A physical question, an observation and an explanatory model](Begin-with-an-electromagnetic-question.lingua#r_1PMJFESWTM62NGP42X33D125WA).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
